  "description": "FUYZIM crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C32 H64 Co2 Er2 N4 O20,2(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Er1 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Co1 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Er2 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Co2 (Co) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.214-3.967 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 96.60-114.62°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C32H64Co2Er2N4O20 (desolvated analytical formula). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
